# clause-runtime-tests — backlog

## Deferred soundness tests

- **Struct-shape assertions.** For every `#[repr(C)]` type in
  `clause-runtime-abi` (`ClauseResult`, `ClauseRuntime`,
  `ClauseDiagnostic`, `AbiSpan`, `AbiToken`, `AbiNode`, …):
  `size_of`, `align_of`, and `offset_of` each public field.
- **Enum discriminant stability.** For every `#[repr(...)]`
  enum (`ClauseResult`, `ClauseDiagnosticKind`, …): assert the
  discriminant value of each variant is what the spec says.
- **ABI version monotonicity.** Assert the `abi_version`
  constant grew monotonically compared to the previous
  committed value (stored in-tree as a sentinel file).

## Deferred Zig-stub integration

- `tests/zig_stub/build.zig` — builds a minimal Zig dylib
  implementing the ABI. Takes `zig-out/lib/libzig_stub.*`.
- `tests/smoke.rs` full round-trip — `RuntimeLoader::load`
  against the stub dylib returns `Ok(handle)`; `handle.execute`
  returns non-empty bytes.
- `tests/diagnostics.rs` — stub dylib records an error;
  driver surfaces it as `clause_ir::Diagnostic`.

## Deferred fuzz / regression

- Fuzz harness over `clause_runtime_execute` (random input
  buffers; asserts no crash, returns valid `ClauseResult`).
- Regression tests — known-bad inputs (NUL bytes,
  zero-length, huge length) each gets a test.
- Crash-recovery tests — runtime aborts, driver detects,
  driver can reload a fresh runtime.

## Non-blocking follow-ups

- `cargo bench` harness against the stub dylib.
- Property-based tests via `proptest` for the ABI
  conversions (`clause_ir` types ↔ `Abi*` mirrors).
